I'm really annoyed that I couldn't think  of an appropriately meta joke told in  this language so news broke earlier  today that there is going to be a  Deadpool animated series being produced  by Donald Glover and it's going to be  appearing on FXX which is right now the  current home of Archer so that should be  nothing but good news this is going on a  network that has no problem with more  adult-oriented animation which means  they're not going to shy away from the  audience that they cultivated with the  movie um and Donald Glover has shown  himself in the past to be a very much a  comic book geek and he he is going to  obviously you know have a reverence for  this character so it's going to be right  up there on screen so why do I not think  this is a very good idea well it's kind  of weird and much like when I saw say  the Blade Runner 2049 trailer and was  like something's not right i had to  reverse engineer to try and figure out  why when i read that news that wasn't  going yeah because that logically should  have been my reaction i'm always  doubting the benefits of animation i  have a sub series called animation  junkie  I love animation and yet I somehow I  think that this is the wrong fit for  this property and I'm going to do my  best to try and explain basically the  short version and I'll expand on this  the short version is that I think  Deadpool will work best the more in  contrast to the world he's in the  character is that's why he works very  well on the comic book page where there  is granted some very ridiculous stuff  going on but it's all being taken so  seriously and you know that whole medium  takes himself so seriously that him  being as a reverend as Diaz is in  contrast to that that's where you get a  lot of the humor from I mean you know  there's the just the randomness of it  too but that's at the heart of the humor  he is the wacky guy in the straight  world and that's very much the case with  the movie as well like everything going  on around with him pretty Poe phase  pretty straightforward he's the one  who's not  so the problem with putting him in a  cartoon is that inherently an animated  world is not as grounded he is not going  to stand out as much in contrast to this  animated setting I mean he he is a  living cartoon and you know that's not  like in a Roger Rabbit sense but I mean  like he is so cartoonish in his behavior  everything else that in that live-action  movie it stands out all the more and it  also stands out and the comic looks for  a similar reason even though visually it  also matches the thing about animation  particularly American animation which is  what this is going to be it's a little  bit different in Japan with in the  history of anime and everything else but  when American animation there just isn't  the same sort of standard of what  reality is so when you insert a wacky  character into a car into a literal  cartoon world it doesn't have that same  contrast where it feels as fun or it  feels as fresh and again to try and  explain why it still works in the comics  even though that is hand-drawn it's  because the comic books as had already  for decades set a standard of we take  this seriously I mean comics hadn't  always been serious but certainly since  the 80s that had been the center we take  this super serious so when this guy was  prepared to tweak the nose of all these  other characters who were taking  themselves so serious in this medium  that took a social series it worked  cartoons as a medium again particularly  American cartoons don't take themselves  very serious so there isn't that baked  in sort of subvert there isn't a baked  in seriousness to the medium that he's  able to subvert so it all has to exist  completely within the world of the  cartoon itself and I'm not saying it  can't do that I'm not saying they can't  create a more serious you know for lack  of a better comparison you know spawn  the animated series kind of world to  draw Deadpool in and there can be some  fun hat in that but that because  animation just doesn't have the inherit  Poe faces of comic books or live-action  film that the contrast isn't it severe  and I feel it's just going to lessen the  character event and just sort of firm  this up for myself I went  and I checked out some of the animated  gif pool stuff that is out there I mean  official stuff I'm not talking fan work  but there was there was an animated  special film DVD thing a Wolverine  versus Hulk that Deadpool appeared it  and that was pretty good but as good as  it was going to be Nolan North poison  for that that worked pretty well um but  you know he was a side character on that  so a little hard to get a gauge on he  also appeared an ultimate spider-man a  voice by Wilfried oh and while he was in  the lane like really grating lis  irritating oh oh that that that was bad  that hurt so and that was then that was  the case where they really leaned into  the excessive cartoonish sense it was  likely trying to make him a Looney Tunes  character and boy it hurt I mean part of  it was just the the pitch on the vocal  performances pour into my ear was not  good um and then you know I also checked  out some of the stuff from the Deadpool  video game and again it's not it's not  bad but there's something about how a  reverend he is in a clinical real-world  setting that I think made it work but I  would argue even better than he does on  the comic book page there's something  about somebody that ridiculous existing  in what seems to be the real world that  to me actually elevates it the the base  level impact of just how ridiculous he  is gets elevated even beyond his comic  book origins so to bring it back to  animation where just the standard of you  know what what is real and what a series  is completely different from live action  or even comic books I just don't I think  it's going to get old and I think it's  going to get old a lot quicker than they  expect it to um yes I mean obviously  look there can be very funny animations  there can be very funny animation names  at adults I mean FX is own Archer IV  zoom proven I love Archer but I think to  myself what I tuned in week after week  to watch him bounce around like Daffy  Duck and that's not me  presuming mood on the thing but the  Deadpool's appeal is how wacky he is and  you put him in a literal cartoon in the  Looney Tunes comparison just it gets all  the stronger now you know I suppose they  give me more why couldn't it be more in  line with how he appeared in in  Wolverine versus Hulk the thing is  though that was a more toned down  version of the character in terms of  embracing the wackiness the fourth wall  breaking all that was gone he just kind  of you just kind of cracked wise now and  then at this point I think the  expectation has been set by the movie  that they're not going to settle for  just that they're going to lean into it  at least as hard as the movie leaned  into it if not more because of animation  you can get away with more and again I  think that's just going to keep in the  character a bit and we're just going to  end up with something closer to his  appearance in ultimate spider-man which  again just whole boy and the thing is  even just beyond the contrast of him  clashing with how serious comic books  are or how serious we expect you know a  real-world set superhero film to be a  lot of the base of his humor aside from  that contrast is just being wacky and  random and cartoon shows right now are  awash in wacky random that's basically  the entirety of Cartoon Network's output  at this point whether it's part of Adult  Swim or for kids that's kind of the  bread and butter of modern animation  right now is is wacky random humor and I  don't know if Deadpool has got to stand  out the way he would have I don't know  maybe ten years ago or so now they just  be saying this is a horrible idea it  can't work no I think it is possible it  could still work but I think there's a  lot stacked against it and until I start  to see footage come out of this it's  something I am going to be really  skeptical of because I think there's a  lot of baggage in terms of what American  animation what people are used to seeing  from American animation that is going to  work against it and I think just the  inherent nature of the character and  where he plays best I think we're going  to find it animation might not be it  certainly not on any kind of an ongoing  long term  so um I'll be curious I'm trying to be  hopeful my opinion on Donald lovers and  involvement it was kind of up down I  haven't seen Atlanta so I don't really  know too much about his output as a  creative force so I can't really judge  that one way or the other but I'm I'm  intrigued but I'm not I'm not jumping up  and down which you know as someone who  loves animation and loves comic books I  should I should be and yet I'm not so I  had to kind of pick apart as to why  wanted to share those thoughts with you  and I'm kind of feeling I'm going to get  called an idiot on this one and I'm  overdue for that I think it's been a  while since people have been calling me  an idiot on math so how much of an idiot  do you think I am whatever your thoughts  are drop something down in the comments  let's talk about it don't forget to like  subscribe check me out on Twitter at  council of geeks give a listen to the  council of geeks podcast or the punch  like a girl podcasts both available on  iTunes and stitcher and until next time  this council is adjourned  [Applause]

